From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giedrius <agnutritions@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:46:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a stream-ticket authorization policy

The media endpoints cannot take a bare [Authorize]: Jellyfin for Android TV
composes stream URLs itself and attaches no credential, so requiring normal
authentication turns every direct play into a server-side HLS remux.

Instead, a short-lived ticket is minted for a session that has already
authenticated through PlaybackInfo, and the stream endpoints accept that ticket.

Registered in ApplicationHost rather than Jellyfin.Server's
AddJellyfinApiAuthorization so the change stays inside the assemblies the local
build already replaces.
---
 .../ApplicationHost.cs                        |  17 +++
 .../StreamAccessPolicy/IStreamTicketStore.cs  |  31 +++++
 .../StreamAccessPolicy/StreamAccessHandler.cs | 100 +++++++++++++++
 .../StreamAccessRequirement.cs                |  23 ++++
 .../StreamAccessPolicy/StreamTicketStore.cs   | 118 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 289 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Jellyfin.Api/Auth/StreamAccessPolicy/IStreamTicketStore.cs
 create mode 100644 Jellyfin.Api/Auth/StreamAccessPolicy/StreamAccessHandler.cs
 create mode 100644 Jellyfin.Api/Auth/StreamAccessPolicy/StreamAccessRequirement.cs
 create mode 100644 Jellyfin.Api/Auth/StreamAccessPolicy/StreamTicketStore.cs

